Files derived from upstream (modified):
  grapheditor/stylesheet.js   Generated from src/main/webapp/styles/default.xml
                              the way upstream's etc/build/build.xml generates
                              Graph-Stylesheet.js (newlines and tabs removed,
                              wrapped in mxUtils.parseXml). Registered as the
                              'default' theme instead of 'default-style2'.

Files written for Easy Diagram (not from upstream):
  config.js                   Sets the globals mxClient/grapheditor read at
                              load time so that nothing is fetched (no
                              resource bundles, stylesheets, stencils or
                              export server).

engine.js does not modify the vendored files. At runtime it changes these
upstream defaults on the prototypes: mxStencilRegistry.dynamicLoading and
allowEval are set to false; mxVertexHandler rotation and custom handles are
switched off; Graph.prototype.addForeignObjectWarning (which adds a
link to drawio.com in SVG exports) is a no-op; the selection/handle colours and edge handle images are
replaced. It also provides two functions that upstream defines in its
diagramly layer, which is not vendored: Editor.guid and
mxGraphView.prototype.redrawEnumerationState (a no-op).

